WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:04.065 --> 00:00:05.934
<i>Previously on</i> Marshals...

2
00:00:06.034 --> 00:00:07.101
- [neighing]
- [Kayce] Hey! Hey!

3
00:00:07.201 --> 00:00:08.303
Hey! Hey!

4
00:00:08.403 --> 00:00:09.937
- Stallion's moving on.
- He's Mom's.

5
00:00:09.938 --> 00:00:11.440
<i>You can't just erase
every memory of her.</i>

6
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.775
I didn't cry
at my dad's funeral.

7
00:00:13.908 --> 00:00:16.610
I was too overwhelmed
by the loss to actually grieve.

8
00:00:16.611 --> 00:00:19.514
[Calvin] <i>It was nice of
your husband and kid to drop by.</i>

9
00:00:19.614 --> 00:00:22.050
You know. building walls
shuts out the people

10
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.485
<i>that you care about.</i>

11
00:00:23.618 --> 00:00:24.853
- [roaring]
- [yells]

12
00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:26.355
[Weaver]
<i>You saved my life.</i>

13
00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:27.822
Let me lend you some hands.

14
00:00:27.922 --> 00:00:29.123
Well. good day for you.
You kept your badge

15
00:00:29.223 --> 00:00:30.359
and you made a new friend.

16
00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:31.860
Saddle up. cowboy.

17
00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.303
♪ "Revelation"
by Ari Kaplan playing ♪

18
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

19
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.022
[neighing]

20
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.497
What part of evolve or die
do you not understand?

21
00:01:08.597 --> 00:01:12.734
<i>♪ Help me to find ♪</i>

22
00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.537
<i>♪ The wisdom ♪</i>

23
00:01:19.173 --> 00:01:23.144
<i>♪ Give me the light ♪</i>

24
00:01:23.244 --> 00:01:28.082
<i>♪ On my darkest night... ♪</i>

25
00:01:28.182 --> 00:01:29.684
[sighs]

26
00:01:29.818 --> 00:01:33.988
<i>♪ I need a revelation ♪</i>

27
00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:37.526
<i>♪ Mm... ♪</i>

28
00:01:37.626 --> 00:01:40.561
Here to check
on your dad's hands.

29
00:01:40.562 --> 00:01:42.330
they're moving the herd.

30
00:01:42.431 --> 00:01:43.765
I was out exploring.

31
00:01:43.865 --> 00:01:45.967
Had a vague memory
of you promising

32
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.603
to give this newbie
an insider's tour.

33
00:01:49.704 --> 00:01:51.573
Pretty sure I said "maybe."

34
00:01:51.706 --> 00:01:52.873
So you'd rather wrestle
that horse than show me

35
00:01:52.874 --> 00:01:54.308
what's so great about Montana?

36
00:01:56.277 --> 00:01:58.246
Try and keep up. [clicks tongue]

37
00:01:58.346 --> 00:02:00.549
♪ majestic music ♪

38
00:02:11.292 --> 00:02:13.528
[Dolly]
Reminds me of the Pyrenees.

39
00:02:13.628 --> 00:02:15.497
[chuckles] Alps. too.

40
00:02:17.265 --> 00:02:19.232
[Kayce] Yeah?
You done a lot of traveling?

41
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:21.069
[Dolly]
Yeah. Growing up.

42
00:02:21.169 --> 00:02:23.638
we'd take family trips
every summer and Christmas.

43
00:02:24.606 --> 00:02:25.740
You?

44
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.242
I had to join the Navy
to see the world.

45
00:02:31.713 --> 00:02:32.981
[Dolly]
And just think.

46
00:02:33.081 --> 00:02:34.949
this was left by a glacier
10.000 years ago.

47
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:37.385
It's also the spot where I took
my brother Jamie's clothes

48
00:02:37.486 --> 00:02:39.954
while he was skinny-dipping.
He had to ride home bare-assed.

49
00:02:40.054 --> 00:02:42.256
[both laugh]

50
00:02:42.356 --> 00:02:44.257
[sighs] Must've been a dream

51
00:02:44.258 --> 00:02:46.828
growing up with
the world's greatest backyard.

52
00:02:48.396 --> 00:02:50.298
Handle that horse pretty well.

53
00:02:51.132 --> 00:02:52.934
Believe it or not.
there are stables in the city.

54
00:02:53.034 --> 00:02:55.369
♪ gentle music ♪

55
00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.276
[Dr. Ginsburg] You said
you'd been experiencing

56
00:03:03.277 --> 00:03:04.713
some neck and shoulder pain?

57
00:03:04.813 --> 00:03:06.047
Some tingling in the hand?

58
00:03:06.147 --> 00:03:08.449
How long have you had
these symptoms?

59
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:11.986
Since the first door
I breached. I just...

60
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.855
I've learned to live with them.

61
00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:17.158
How many deployments
did you have?

62
00:03:18.226 --> 00:03:20.962
More than I can remember. literally.

63
00:03:22.463 --> 00:03:26.501
Well. we'll run some tests.
try to find you some answers.

64
00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.338
Okay.

65
00:03:30.438 --> 00:03:32.907
♪ dramatic music ♪

66
00:03:39.447 --> 00:03:41.315
[woman]
See you later.

67
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.318
[Jared]
Cal?

68
00:03:44.418 --> 00:03:46.020
What are you doing here?

69
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.622
Belle hasn't mentioned
your team is

70
00:03:47.722 --> 00:03:48.823
running down fugitive doctors.

71
00:03:48.923 --> 00:03:50.124
- [chuckles]
- Hey. Jared.

72
00:03:50.224 --> 00:03:52.861
Uh. nah. I was just. um.
getting a checkup.

73
00:03:54.262 --> 00:03:57.832
Yeah. I was at a work lunch.
Should get back to the office.

74
00:03:57.932 --> 00:04:00.333
Right. It's good seeing you.

75
00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.335
Yeah.

76
00:04:01.469 --> 00:04:03.738
♪ low. dramatic music ♪

77
00:04:17.118 --> 00:04:18.386
Your dad make you
uproot your life

78
00:04:18.486 --> 00:04:19.720
to move all the way out here?

79
00:04:19.721 --> 00:04:22.856
[chuckles]
I'm a grown woman.

80
00:04:22.857 --> 00:04:25.226
Can't make me do anything.

81
00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.729
I'm here because I love him.

82
00:04:27.829 --> 00:04:30.431
and because he made me partner
in his new cattle venture.

83
00:04:30.531 --> 00:04:31.733
[Weaver groaning]

84
00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:32.866
[Dolly]
Dad. what're you doing here?

85
00:04:32.867 --> 00:04:34.903
[exhales]

86
00:04:35.003 --> 00:04:37.739
[Weaver]
Kayce broke my leg.

87
00:04:37.872 --> 00:04:39.874
Had to make sure
you were safe. pumpkin.

88
00:04:39.974 --> 00:04:42.376
- [chuckles]
- I believe

89
00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:44.646
you brought me a hat.
last time I saw you.

90
00:04:45.914 --> 00:04:49.350
Allow me to return the favor.
[chuckles]

91
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.854
It's good to see you up
on your feet so soon. sir.

92
00:04:52.954 --> 00:04:55.389
No days off on the ranch. right?

93
00:04:55.489 --> 00:04:58.760
And I healed enough
I managed to bag an elk.

94
00:04:58.893 --> 00:05:02.797
I figured I'd make dinner.
pay down my debt to you.

95
00:05:04.232 --> 00:05:06.735
Well. I know better than to
refuse an offer from a Weaver.

96
00:05:06.835 --> 00:05:08.236
[Dolly and Weaver chuckle]

97
00:05:08.336 --> 00:05:10.438
[Weaver]
Great.

98
00:05:10.538 --> 00:05:13.975
[up-tempo rock music playing]

99
00:05:14.075 --> 00:05:16.711
[Maddie laughs]
Here... Here you go. Miles.

100
00:05:16.811 --> 00:05:18.412
Uh. the tea was a little tart.

101
00:05:18.512 --> 00:05:21.448
so I-I spiked it
with a sugar cube.

102
00:05:21.449 --> 00:05:23.618
- Appreciate it.
- [chuckles]

103
00:05:24.485 --> 00:05:26.921
<i>♪ I keep the faith. oh. man ♪</i>

104
00:05:27.055 --> 00:05:28.956
<i>♪ Million dollar
doubt about it... ♪</i>

105
00:05:28.957 --> 00:05:30.759
Feel bad rolling you
on Mom's night out.

106
00:05:30.892 --> 00:05:32.927
[Belle]
Eh...

107
00:05:33.027 --> 00:05:36.464
Jared and Braxton left
for a father-son camping trip.

108
00:05:36.597 --> 00:05:39.533
so I got all night
to take your money.

109
00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:41.469
Mm. Who you betting on?

110
00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:43.838
After seeing Belle
as a biker chick.

111
00:05:43.938 --> 00:05:46.274
I got no doubt
she's got some hustler in her.

112
00:05:46.374 --> 00:05:47.941
- Mm.
- [Andrea chuckles]

113
00:05:47.942 --> 00:05:49.643
My money's on Miles.

114
00:05:49.644 --> 00:05:53.147
Broken Rock's luck is turning.
thanks to its guardian angel.

115
00:05:53.281 --> 00:05:56.950
Sabrina. these are my teammates.
Belle and Andrea.

116
00:05:56.951 --> 00:05:58.186
They helped find
the missing girls.

117
00:05:58.286 --> 00:06:00.988
Well. look at you.
sharing credit.

118
00:06:00.989 --> 00:06:02.190
You know.
for a former college athlete.

119
00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.291
you have a pretty small ego.

120
00:06:03.391 --> 00:06:05.459
"College athlete" is a stretch.

121
00:06:05.593 --> 00:06:09.130
All state tight end
and linebacker. full ride

122
00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.965
- to a D1 program.
- [Andrea] Damn. Miles.

123
00:06:11.065 --> 00:06:13.501
I knew you played. but
I didn't know you were a player.

124
00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:15.970
I wasn't. Dropped the ball.

125
00:06:16.104 --> 00:06:18.306
Miles and the coach didn't
see eye to eye.

126
00:06:18.406 --> 00:06:20.074
Dust Cloud being Dust Cloud.

127
00:06:20.174 --> 00:06:21.508
I've mellowed.

128
00:06:21.509 --> 00:06:23.044
Hopefully not too much.

129
00:06:25.313 --> 00:06:27.448
- [clears throat]
- Nice meeting you.

130
00:06:27.548 --> 00:06:30.484
Miles's friends.
Give me a call sometime. Miles.

131
00:06:30.618 --> 00:06:34.488
<i>♪ And if I don't win. hell.
I'll try again tomorrow... ♪</i>

132
00:06:34.622 --> 00:06:36.157
[Sabrina laughs]

133
00:06:36.257 --> 00:06:39.527
All right. This does bring up
a very important question.

134
00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.429
Are you dating anyone?

135
00:06:41.529 --> 00:06:43.331
No. [chuckles]

136
00:06:43.431 --> 00:06:44.733
[Miles clears throat]

137
00:06:44.833 --> 00:06:46.167
You like someone.

138
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.668
It's complicated.

139
00:06:47.769 --> 00:06:50.872
- [Andrea gasps]
- She's not from where I'm from.

140
00:06:50.972 --> 00:06:53.506
- So?
- So. like my football career.

141
00:06:53.507 --> 00:06:55.276
it's probably not meant to be.

142
00:06:56.945 --> 00:06:58.246
[Miles clears throat]

143
00:07:01.415 --> 00:07:03.216
I know. it was delicious.

144
00:07:03.217 --> 00:07:04.886
I think I want to come back
next week.

145
00:07:04.986 --> 00:07:07.555
- Yeah. We will. [chuckles]
- Yeah. good. Good. good. good.

146
00:07:10.324 --> 00:07:11.726
I forgot the leftovers.

147
00:07:11.826 --> 00:07:13.194
[Pauline chuckles]
Blake...

148
00:07:13.327 --> 00:07:14.695
All right. I'm going back.

149
00:07:14.796 --> 00:07:16.865
Shoot. I left my glasses inside.
Just be a minute.

150
00:07:16.998 --> 00:07:18.432
[valet] I'll keep it running.
Your Honor.

151
00:07:20.334 --> 00:07:22.536
[car alarm blaring]

152
00:07:29.143 --> 00:07:31.312
♪ soaring. dynamic music ♪

153
00:07:55.937 --> 00:07:58.106
♪

154
00:08:03.177 --> 00:08:06.915
Good job. sir.
Most people overcook elk.

155
00:08:07.015 --> 00:08:09.082
Mm. Dad's the chef
in the family.

156
00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:12.053
I got an unwanted promotion
to house cook.

157
00:08:12.153 --> 00:08:13.754
I can't compete with you.

158
00:08:14.555 --> 00:08:15.755
How I feel
about you and your family

159
00:08:15.756 --> 00:08:16.958
when it comes to ranching.

160
00:08:17.058 --> 00:08:19.127
Hmm. Why he pays
a team of brainiacs

161
00:08:19.227 --> 00:08:20.228
with ag degrees to help.

162
00:08:20.328 --> 00:08:21.896
[Weaver]
Doing more than helping.

163
00:08:21.996 --> 00:08:23.764
They've pointed me
toward some technologies

164
00:08:23.865 --> 00:08:26.133
to up my chances for success.

165
00:08:26.134 --> 00:08:28.970
Well. I was raised to believe
the old ways are the right ways.

166
00:08:29.103 --> 00:08:31.772
[Weaver] From what I hear.
the old ways included

167
00:08:31.873 --> 00:08:34.375
the Yellowstone never turning
a profit.

168
00:08:34.475 --> 00:08:37.812
[scoffs] Well. the way of life
is the true reward

169
00:08:37.946 --> 00:08:39.646
when it comes to ranching. sir.

170
00:08:39.647 --> 00:08:41.950
[chuckles]
Not with my investors.

171
00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.452
If-if I can put my thumb
on the scale.

172
00:08:44.552 --> 00:08:45.619
why wouldn't I?

173
00:08:45.719 --> 00:08:48.155
DNA marker testing
helped me pick

174
00:08:48.156 --> 00:08:49.457
the most productive cattle
to start with.

175
00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.459
and now.
I'm tracking them using RFID

176
00:08:51.592 --> 00:08:53.327
to keep my labor costs down.

177
00:08:53.427 --> 00:08:56.129
Sounds like a hefty
up-front cost.

178
00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.832
That's why I spread the risk.

179
00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:01.669
Offer each head
as an individual asset

180
00:09:01.802 --> 00:09:03.637
folks can invest in.

181
00:09:03.737 --> 00:09:06.941
That working capital
increases my valuation.

182
00:09:07.041 --> 00:09:08.509
[chuckles]

183
00:09:08.609 --> 00:09:10.644
You and my sister'd get along.

184
00:09:10.778 --> 00:09:13.915
I'm in it
for the long haul. Kayce.

185
00:09:14.015 --> 00:09:15.482
More land. more cattle.

186
00:09:15.483 --> 00:09:17.818
That's how I attract
more investors.

187
00:09:19.187 --> 00:09:21.322
I would love

188
00:09:21.422 --> 00:09:24.425
to make East Camp
part of my operation.

189
00:09:24.525 --> 00:09:27.261
♪ tense. dramatic music ♪

190
00:09:30.464 --> 00:09:32.266
You want to buy my ranch?

191
00:09:35.769 --> 00:09:37.238
[wry chuckle]

192
00:09:37.338 --> 00:09:40.373
Geez. Dad. give him dessert
before asking him into bed.

193
00:09:40.374 --> 00:09:43.444
I'm direct when I see
something I want.

194
00:09:45.146 --> 00:09:48.216
Hmm. Thank you for dinner.

195
00:09:50.051 --> 00:09:52.052
Uh. let us help clean up.

196
00:09:52.053 --> 00:09:55.523
No. dishes are one thing
I can handle in the kitchen.

197
00:09:55.623 --> 00:09:59.560
I meant no. uh. no offense.

198
00:09:59.693 --> 00:10:02.363
We can both come out winners.

199
00:10:02.463 --> 00:10:04.532
Think it over.

200
00:10:12.974 --> 00:10:15.243
♪ low. dramatic music ♪

201
00:10:18.346 --> 00:10:19.913
- [sighs]
- Was that some sort of plan

202
00:10:19.914 --> 00:10:22.383
to soften me up
so your dad could make an offer

203
00:10:22.516 --> 00:10:23.717
on East Camp?

204
00:10:23.851 --> 00:10:26.254
I was as blindsided as you.

205
00:10:27.255 --> 00:10:30.390
It's why my family never talks
business at the dinner table.

206
00:10:30.391 --> 00:10:32.260
[sighs]

207
00:10:36.564 --> 00:10:38.699
I'm sorry.

208
00:10:41.902 --> 00:10:44.272
We were having fun
until he ruined it.

209
00:10:44.372 --> 00:10:46.707
Weren't we?

210
00:10:47.741 --> 00:10:48.943
Yeah.

211
00:10:49.043 --> 00:10:51.445
Thank you for a lovely day.

212
00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.990
Good night.

213
00:11:13.134 --> 00:11:16.070
Hey. Got something
you want to tell me?

214
00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:17.305
About what?

215
00:11:17.405 --> 00:11:19.907
Ghosting us at the bar
last night.

216
00:11:20.008 --> 00:11:22.643
Ah. [scoffs] Yeah.
Day got away from me. My bad.

217
00:11:22.743 --> 00:11:24.145
Uh-huh.

218
00:11:24.278 --> 00:11:25.278
Hey. Gifford called.

219
00:11:25.279 --> 00:11:26.813
We've got something.

220
00:11:26.814 --> 00:11:28.983
Federal Judge Pauline Ayers
and her husband Blake

221
00:11:29.083 --> 00:11:31.285
- survived a car bomb attack.
- [Calvin] Yeah. I saw that.

222
00:11:31.419 --> 00:11:32.953
The valet wasn't so lucky.

223
00:11:33.054 --> 00:11:34.722
You got any leads on a suspect?

224
00:11:34.822 --> 00:11:38.792
[groans] A federal judge likely
has a long list of enemies.

225
00:11:38.892 --> 00:11:41.729
Clint Gallo.
Threatened revenge ten years ago

226
00:11:41.829 --> 00:11:43.131
when Ayers sentenced him
to prison

227
00:11:43.264 --> 00:11:45.333
for the bombing
of a women's health center.

228
00:11:45.433 --> 00:11:47.135
Paroled last month.
Missed a check-in

229
00:11:47.235 --> 00:11:48.269
with his P.O. last week.

230
00:11:48.369 --> 00:11:49.970
Well. that makes him a fugitive.

231
00:11:50.104 --> 00:11:52.306
Yeah. The FBI's got the lead on
the bombing. but Gallo's ours.

232
00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.376
Judicial protection falls under
the Marshals' purview.

233
00:11:55.476 --> 00:11:56.910
Are we watching over Ayers?

234
00:11:57.011 --> 00:11:59.347
And her family. until
her attacker's in custody.

235
00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:02.182
Cowboy and I can hunt down
the ex-con while the rest of you

236
00:12:02.183 --> 00:12:03.851
shack up with the happy family?

237
00:12:04.985 --> 00:12:07.088
♪ dramatic music ♪

238
00:12:08.022 --> 00:12:11.825
Yeah. Last thing we need
is an open season on judges.

239
00:12:18.666 --> 00:12:20.000
[Calvin]
I know it feels like

240
00:12:20.101 --> 00:12:21.702
we're punishing
the victims here. but...

241
00:12:21.802 --> 00:12:23.536
but given the bomber
knew your pattern of life.

242
00:12:23.537 --> 00:12:24.871
we're-we're gonna
have to restrict

243
00:12:24.872 --> 00:12:26.207
your family's movements.

244
00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.742
Your marshal doing
the security sweep is gonna

245
00:12:28.842 --> 00:12:30.009
spook our neighbors.

246
00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.980
Uh. you...
do you have any leads?

247
00:12:33.081 --> 00:12:35.383
[Belle]
We're eyeing a violent convict

248
00:12:35.516 --> 00:12:37.017
you sent away years ago.

249
00:12:37.118 --> 00:12:41.054
Oh. Well. that
really narrows it down.

250
00:12:41.055 --> 00:12:42.855
We're gonna do our best to stay
out of your hair. Your Honor.

251
00:12:42.856 --> 00:12:45.725
Oh. knock that
"Your Honor" crap off.

252
00:12:45.726 --> 00:12:47.194
Hey.

253
00:12:47.195 --> 00:12:50.331
Oh. Magic City
Nonprofit of the Year

254
00:12:50.431 --> 00:12:53.501
2023. Chiron's Care.

255
00:12:53.601 --> 00:12:55.336
[Blake] I'm the. uh.
executive director.

256
00:12:55.436 --> 00:12:56.704
We get medical equipment

257
00:12:56.804 --> 00:12:58.639
to underserved communities
around the world.

258
00:12:58.739 --> 00:13:00.574
He's the softie.
I'm the hard-ass.

259
00:13:00.708 --> 00:13:01.675
[others chuckle]

260
00:13:01.775 --> 00:13:03.944
Well. if you need
dental supplies.

261
00:13:04.044 --> 00:13:05.313
I can connect you to my husband.

262
00:13:05.413 --> 00:13:07.248
He's a do-gooder. too.

263
00:13:07.381 --> 00:13:09.950
[Fallon] Franny says Lulu
wants the ticket

264
00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.919
to MountainLoaf if I can't go.

265
00:13:12.019 --> 00:13:14.222
The. uh. music festival
next month?

266
00:13:14.322 --> 00:13:15.556
Yeah.

267
00:13:15.689 --> 00:13:18.058
Well. honey. if you're
still under protection

268
00:13:18.192 --> 00:13:20.994
by then.
we have failed at our job.

269
00:13:21.095 --> 00:13:24.031
[Pauline] Even if you succeed.
Blake and I

270
00:13:24.132 --> 00:13:26.100
haven't said that Fallon can go.

271
00:13:26.234 --> 00:13:28.436
♪ dramatic music ♪

272
00:13:29.903 --> 00:13:31.071
My mistake.

273
00:13:31.939 --> 00:13:33.374
[Fallon sighs]

274
00:13:34.875 --> 00:13:37.410
This is where
Gallo's girlfriend lives?

275
00:13:37.411 --> 00:13:39.779
Guess she's got a kink
for convicts.

276
00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.615
Okay. so. Gallo took a shot
at the judge

277
00:13:41.749 --> 00:13:43.250
after serving ten years?

278
00:13:43.251 --> 00:13:44.818
[Andrea]
Values vengeance over freedom.

279
00:13:44.918 --> 00:13:46.420
- Seems like a trade you'd make.
- [indistinct chatter]

280
00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:47.955
Hey.

281
00:13:48.055 --> 00:13:50.458
Clint Gallo?

282
00:13:50.558 --> 00:13:52.926
♪ intense. dramatic music ♪

283
00:13:54.462 --> 00:13:55.929
[Kayce]
U.S. Marshals!

284
00:14:01.835 --> 00:14:03.070
[Gallo groans]

285
00:14:04.938 --> 00:14:07.140
[sighs] Tossed him
like an angry bronc.

286
00:14:07.141 --> 00:14:08.942
You're sounding more Montanan
every day.

287
00:14:09.076 --> 00:14:11.779
- [laughs. sighs]
- [sighs]

288
00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.649
You know. much of my work
is confidential.

289
00:14:15.749 --> 00:14:17.451
[Miles] The Fusion Center
won't break privilege.

290
00:14:17.551 --> 00:14:20.388
they'll just analyze the threats
you've gotten.

291
00:14:20.488 --> 00:14:23.090
[Blake]
Hope they're working in shifts.

292
00:14:24.057 --> 00:14:25.759
Your husband give you
a hard time

293
00:14:25.859 --> 00:14:27.795
for going after the worst of us?

294
00:14:28.629 --> 00:14:31.498
It's a constant negotiation.

295
00:14:31.499 --> 00:14:34.535
but we always find
common ground.

296
00:14:35.636 --> 00:14:38.105
Unfortunately for me.
judges don't negotiate.

297
00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:40.308
[chuckles]

298
00:14:40.408 --> 00:14:41.875
♪ gentle music ♪

299
00:14:41.975 --> 00:14:43.477
[Calvin]
Your Honor... Ma'am?

300
00:14:43.611 --> 00:14:45.979
We're gonna need you to stay
where we can keep eyes on.

301
00:14:46.079 --> 00:14:47.481
I need to use the bathroom.

302
00:14:47.581 --> 00:14:49.817
[Calvin] Use your daughter's.
There's no windows.

303
00:14:49.917 --> 00:14:51.652
Stay out of there.
I'm tie-dyeing a dress

304
00:14:51.752 --> 00:14:52.853
for MountainLoaf.

305
00:14:52.953 --> 00:14:54.588
[sighs] Don't get
ahead of yourself.

306
00:14:54.688 --> 00:14:56.324
[Blake] We should let her go.
have some normal teenage fun

307
00:14:56.457 --> 00:14:58.058
after all this.

308
00:14:58.158 --> 00:14:59.460
Hey. you heard Mom.

309
00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.862
No chance Maximum Pauline
shows me any leniency.

310
00:15:01.962 --> 00:15:05.199
Great. I'm the bad guy. Again.

311
00:15:05.333 --> 00:15:07.668
♪ melancholy music ♪

312
00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.240
You think we should warn them
the last thing they want

313
00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.275
is their daughter
picking sides between them?

314
00:15:14.375 --> 00:15:17.578
She's got enough on her plate
with someone trying to kill her.

315
00:15:18.846 --> 00:15:21.782
But if you know something
that affects somebody's family.

316
00:15:21.882 --> 00:15:24.485
I mean.
you should say something. right?

317
00:15:25.319 --> 00:15:29.189
Family drama should stay
in the family.

318
00:15:33.861 --> 00:15:35.763
[Andrea]
<i>Threatened the judge last decade</i>

319
00:15:35.863 --> 00:15:37.731
<i>and enacted your vengeance
last night.</i>

320
00:15:37.865 --> 00:15:39.900
You sure can hold a grudge.
I'll give you that.

321
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.403
- Ayers is dead?
- Nope. but a valet is.

322
00:15:43.404 --> 00:15:47.975
I was at Teresa's all yesterday.
She'll vouch for me.

323
00:15:48.075 --> 00:15:50.544
Doesn't matter.
When the bomb went off

324
00:15:50.678 --> 00:15:53.714
and when it was planted
are two different timelines.

325
00:15:53.814 --> 00:15:56.817
I got better things to do
than settle some old score.

326
00:15:56.917 --> 00:15:59.687
Way she dropped the hammer.
cops are getting

327
00:15:59.787 --> 00:16:01.755
pretty lazy if they think
I'm the only one

328
00:16:01.889 --> 00:16:03.090
dreamt of murdering her.

329
00:16:03.223 --> 00:16:06.260
♪ dramatic music ♪

330
00:16:08.829 --> 00:16:11.565
I'm trapped in my home.
like Elsa.

331
00:16:11.699 --> 00:16:14.268
No one wants
to hear this. honey.

332
00:16:14.368 --> 00:16:17.104
Maybe this is a blessing
in disguise.

333
00:16:17.237 --> 00:16:21.842
A chance to put family first.
the way you talk about. Hmm?

334
00:16:24.512 --> 00:16:27.515
That guy sure seems thirsty
for his wife's attention.

335
00:16:27.615 --> 00:16:30.784
What's with your need to play
Dr. Phil with them?

336
00:16:30.884 --> 00:16:33.586
Nothing. We just both know
that putting all in at work

337
00:16:33.587 --> 00:16:35.423
can fracture relationships.

338
00:16:38.091 --> 00:16:39.860
Speak for yourself.

339
00:16:42.296 --> 00:16:43.664
- Fallon. no!
- [alarms wailing]

340
00:16:43.764 --> 00:16:45.766
[Calvin]
Get down. get down!

341
00:16:45.866 --> 00:16:48.602
- Away from the window.
- [gunshot]

342
00:16:53.006 --> 00:16:54.274
It's okay. baby. You're fine.

343
00:16:54.408 --> 00:16:56.109
Someone's trying to kill you.
Nothing is fine.

344
00:16:56.209 --> 00:16:57.244
[banging on door]

345
00:16:57.345 --> 00:16:59.046
[Belle]
Blue. blue.

346
00:17:00.414 --> 00:17:02.983
[Calvin]
So? Any trace of the shooter?

347
00:17:03.083 --> 00:17:04.117
[Belle]
Negative.

348
00:17:04.217 --> 00:17:06.152
Only place shots
could've come from

349
00:17:06.153 --> 00:17:07.488
is the parking garage
across the street.

350
00:17:07.621 --> 00:17:09.623
[Miles]
Didn't find any casings.

351
00:17:09.723 --> 00:17:11.592
Shooter cleared out too fast
to be on foot.

352
00:17:11.692 --> 00:17:13.026
We're getting security footage.

353
00:17:13.126 --> 00:17:16.128
Does Gallo's sheet have
any long guns work?

354
00:17:16.129 --> 00:17:17.998
Kayce and Andrea apprehended him

355
00:17:18.131 --> 00:17:20.132
well before
these shots were fired.

356
00:17:20.133 --> 00:17:21.469
Okay. well.
if he's not our shooter.

357
00:17:21.569 --> 00:17:23.337
then we can't still like him
for the bombing.

358
00:17:23.437 --> 00:17:25.305
Only thing certain is that
the assassin knows

359
00:17:25.406 --> 00:17:26.673
where the judge is. so...

360
00:17:26.674 --> 00:17:27.975
Listen up. y'all.

361
00:17:28.075 --> 00:17:30.344
Ayers family.
there's a change of venue. okay?

362
00:17:30.478 --> 00:17:32.480
You're coming to our house now.

363
00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.147
Local PD is coming in
to take over the crime scene.

364
00:17:35.148 --> 00:17:37.316
I can hold here
in case anything comes up.

365
00:17:37.317 --> 00:17:39.653
[Pauline] There must be some way
that you can keep me safe

366
00:17:39.753 --> 00:17:42.188
and not make my family
feel like prisoners.

367
00:17:42.189 --> 00:17:45.325
♪ tense. dramatic music ♪

368
00:17:46.794 --> 00:17:49.062
Hey. I know a place

369
00:17:49.162 --> 00:17:51.331
off-grid. okay.
that we can tuck these two away.

370
00:17:51.432 --> 00:17:53.667
Okay? But you're coming with us.

371
00:17:53.801 --> 00:17:54.702
Yeah.

372
00:17:54.835 --> 00:17:57.237
Okay. come on. y'all. Let's go.

373
00:17:57.337 --> 00:17:58.839
It's gonna be okay.

374
00:17:58.939 --> 00:18:01.675
Takes an assassination attempt
on a judge

375
00:18:01.775 --> 00:18:03.444
for an invite to your place.

376
00:18:03.544 --> 00:18:05.446
I think you're confusing
an order from Cal

377
00:18:05.546 --> 00:18:06.847
for a social gathering.

378
00:18:06.947 --> 00:18:09.182
Weaver Ranch?

379
00:18:09.282 --> 00:18:11.719
I see who your social
invitations are reserved for.

380
00:18:11.819 --> 00:18:13.120
[door opens]

381
00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.522
[Calvin]
Blue. blue.

382
00:18:14.655 --> 00:18:17.189
Blake. Fallon.
I want you to meet

383
00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:19.191
Deputy Marshals Dutton and Cruz.

384
00:18:19.192 --> 00:18:21.395
Apologies for the intrusion.

385
00:18:21.495 --> 00:18:22.696
Oh. don't apologize.

386
00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.364
I understand
how you must be feeling.

387
00:18:24.498 --> 00:18:26.033
I believe you do.

388
00:18:26.166 --> 00:18:27.901
What's that mean?

389
00:18:28.702 --> 00:18:32.072
It means we're in good hands
with Deputy Marshal Dutton.

390
00:18:32.205 --> 00:18:33.807
[Fallon]
Good. Then he can find

391
00:18:33.907 --> 00:18:37.277
who's trying to kill Mom
and we can go home.

392
00:18:47.087 --> 00:18:49.923
[Andrea] If Gallo isn't our guy.
then any new theories on who is?

393
00:18:50.023 --> 00:18:52.426
Yeah.
FBI forensics have concluded

394
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.261
that the bomb from the car
is more commonly seen

395
00:18:54.361 --> 00:18:56.697
in the African Sahel
than in domestic terrorism.

396
00:18:56.797 --> 00:18:59.231
[Kayce]
Yeah. that type of bomb making

397
00:18:59.232 --> 00:19:01.001
and sniper skillset
feels military.

398
00:19:01.101 --> 00:19:02.770
Agree. That's why
we're cross-referencing

399
00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.939
the judge's sentencing records
with military jackets. but

400
00:19:06.073 --> 00:19:09.610
till we find that assassin.
y'all keep your heads down.

401
00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:13.747
[door closes]

402
00:19:13.847 --> 00:19:15.916
Was it Tom or Dolly
who came over?

403
00:19:16.049 --> 00:19:17.918
[scoffs]

404
00:19:18.051 --> 00:19:21.054
Sounds like we'll be here
for a while. You'll tell me.

405
00:19:21.154 --> 00:19:23.957
- I'm doing a security sweep.
- [chuckles]

406
00:19:24.091 --> 00:19:25.693
- [indistinct chatter]
- Okay.

407
00:19:25.793 --> 00:19:28.128
[Park] Security cams caught
a red van entering the garage

408
00:19:28.228 --> 00:19:30.664
15 minutes before the shooting
and exiting shortly after.

409
00:19:30.764 --> 00:19:32.533
No plates. but we're
sending you the footage.

410
00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.802
Take what we can get
at this point.

411
00:19:34.935 --> 00:19:36.302
[Park]
And my team found these

412
00:19:36.303 --> 00:19:39.006
hidden in the wall
near the bullet hits.

413
00:19:44.411 --> 00:19:46.780
Looks like the judge's husband.

414
00:19:48.315 --> 00:19:50.851
Why's a nonprofit director
need an alias?

415
00:19:51.719 --> 00:19:53.787
[Calvin] I'll give you
some privacy. ma'am.

416
00:19:57.257 --> 00:20:00.093
Well. judge is settled in.

417
00:20:00.894 --> 00:20:03.831
You figured out if her husband's
Jason Bourne?

418
00:20:04.798 --> 00:20:08.467
Only his real passport
has been used for travel.

419
00:20:08.468 --> 00:20:11.304
Then why all the other
phony IDs?

420
00:20:12.139 --> 00:20:13.607
Finances.

421
00:20:14.407 --> 00:20:17.645
Account attached to one of them
shows money moving from Blake

422
00:20:17.745 --> 00:20:19.847
through shell corporations

423
00:20:19.947 --> 00:20:23.150
to Equatorial Guinea and back.

424
00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.819
Wait. Equatorial Guinea's
part of the Sahel.

425
00:20:25.919 --> 00:20:29.189
where the car bomb's
tradecraft points to.

426
00:20:36.597 --> 00:20:38.398
Well. maybe
he's masking the payment

427
00:20:38.498 --> 00:20:40.166
for a hit out on his wife.

428
00:20:40.167 --> 00:20:42.535
You think he is a suspect now?

429
00:20:42.536 --> 00:20:46.338
He was with her during
both assassination attempts.

430
00:20:46.339 --> 00:20:48.642
I mean. being in the line
of fire's a hell of an alibi.

431
00:20:48.742 --> 00:20:51.545
Okay. What's his motive?

432
00:20:51.679 --> 00:20:53.714
I mean. the marriage has
run its course.

433
00:20:53.847 --> 00:20:55.683
and he'd rather collect
life insurance

434
00:20:55.816 --> 00:20:58.418
than face a judge
in divorce court.

435
00:20:59.186 --> 00:21:01.854
I know a broken relationship
when I see one.

436
00:21:01.855 --> 00:21:04.157
♪ dramatic music ♪

437
00:21:08.128 --> 00:21:09.763
Do you have anything to eat?

438
00:21:11.231 --> 00:21:13.934
Uh... Got some elk steaks.

439
00:21:14.702 --> 00:21:17.004
I spotted some Uncrustables
in the fridge

440
00:21:17.104 --> 00:21:19.239
for the non-cavemen.

441
00:21:26.747 --> 00:21:28.081
[refrigerator door closes]

442
00:21:32.686 --> 00:21:34.855
I'm having trouble
with cell service.

443
00:21:34.955 --> 00:21:37.057
Downside of living
in the 19th century.

444
00:21:37.858 --> 00:21:40.393
The. uh. porch might get you
a bar or two.

445
00:21:40.493 --> 00:21:42.663
♪ somber music ♪

446
00:21:45.398 --> 00:21:47.234
[sighs]

447
00:21:48.702 --> 00:21:51.404
How you holding up?

448
00:21:52.439 --> 00:21:55.943
Some psycho wanting my mom dead
is kind of messing with me.

449
00:21:57.911 --> 00:21:59.246
We get it.

450
00:21:59.346 --> 00:22:01.581
Both of our dads died
because of their job.

451
00:22:04.284 --> 00:22:05.452
That's so awful.

452
00:22:06.353 --> 00:22:08.989
[Andrea] I lost my dad
in the line of duty.

453
00:22:09.089 --> 00:22:11.224
and Kayce's dad was
the governor.

454
00:22:11.324 --> 00:22:13.060
They find their killers?

455
00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:16.630
Chance to find my dad's gets me
out of bed in the morning.

456
00:22:17.597 --> 00:22:19.399
People on social media
were obsessed

457
00:22:19.499 --> 00:22:21.133
with trying to solve
your dad's murder.

458
00:22:21.134 --> 00:22:22.602
Hmm.

459
00:22:23.536 --> 00:22:26.472
- I don't think about it much.
- [Andrea] Oh. come on.

460
00:22:26.473 --> 00:22:28.742
You go man on fire
for victims you've never met.

461
00:22:28.842 --> 00:22:30.811
You're telling me you don't have
a list of suspects?

462
00:22:31.645 --> 00:22:34.814
Heard something about...
private contractors.

463
00:22:34.815 --> 00:22:36.983
[Fallon] Is it wrong
that I want something

464
00:22:36.984 --> 00:22:39.451
bad to happen
to whoever's after my mom?

465
00:22:39.452 --> 00:22:42.121
There's a big difference
between craving vengeance

466
00:22:42.122 --> 00:22:43.523
and getting it.

467
00:22:44.424 --> 00:22:46.625
[Andrea]
I think about getting it plenty.

468
00:22:46.626 --> 00:22:48.628
This was my dad's.

469
00:22:48.729 --> 00:22:51.498
I carry it on the off chance
I ever meet his killer.

470
00:22:51.598 --> 00:22:53.366
But mostly it just gives me
a sense of control

471
00:22:53.466 --> 00:22:56.003
over the thing that owns me.

472
00:22:58.005 --> 00:23:01.074
[phone buzzing]

473
00:23:04.011 --> 00:23:05.813
- [Kayce] Yeah?
- [Calvin over phone] <i>Coyo.</i>

474
00:23:05.913 --> 00:23:08.180
husband's starting
to look shady.

475
00:23:08.181 --> 00:23:10.583
He's got aliases.
international payments.

476
00:23:10.684 --> 00:23:12.786
<i>I think he could be involved.</i>

477
00:23:12.886 --> 00:23:14.653
Well. there's a twist.

478
00:23:14.654 --> 00:23:16.989
<i>I'm gonna need you
to feel him out. okay?</i>

479
00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:18.258
Yeah.

480
00:23:18.358 --> 00:23:20.560
♪ suspenseful music ♪

481
00:23:25.398 --> 00:23:26.867
Blake?

482
00:23:32.239 --> 00:23:33.807
Blake?

483
00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:38.411
Blake?

484
00:23:42.649 --> 00:23:44.583
How could he be missing? He was
under your team's protection.

485
00:23:44.584 --> 00:23:46.586
My marshals think that
he left on his own.

486
00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:48.588
Fallon is his whole life.
He wouldn't.

487
00:23:48.688 --> 00:23:50.924
Well. we have security footage

488
00:23:51.024 --> 00:23:52.993
from your husband's
disappearance.

489
00:23:53.093 --> 00:23:55.762
♪ tense. dramatic music ♪

490
00:23:55.763 --> 00:23:58.531
Does the name Joseph Petit
mean anything to you?

491
00:23:59.432 --> 00:24:00.600
No.

492
00:24:00.734 --> 00:24:04.270
Joseph Petit is an alias
your husband uses.

493
00:24:04.271 --> 00:24:06.807
Alias? I don't follow.

494
00:24:06.907 --> 00:24:08.241
Your husband keeps
false passports

495
00:24:08.375 --> 00:24:10.310
in a wall in your home.
You aware of that?

496
00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:15.482
And is there anything else
he could be hiding?

497
00:24:15.582 --> 00:24:18.518
Are you investigating
my husband?

498
00:24:22.522 --> 00:24:24.057
Should we be?

499
00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:29.396
We pulled this
from surveillance cameras

500
00:24:29.496 --> 00:24:31.231
on our colleague's ranch.

501
00:24:34.034 --> 00:24:37.104
Seems like
he was expecting them.

502
00:24:43.243 --> 00:24:44.812
[inhales shakily]

503
00:24:44.912 --> 00:24:47.114
They kidnapped him?

504
00:24:47.247 --> 00:24:50.383
Has he been the target
all along?

505
00:24:51.251 --> 00:24:53.053
It's possible.

506
00:24:53.153 --> 00:24:54.454
But why?

507
00:24:54.554 --> 00:24:57.324
We were hoping you...
you might know. Your Honor.

508
00:24:57.424 --> 00:25:00.293
My husband of 25 years

509
00:25:00.393 --> 00:25:02.495
has been living
a secret life. so

510
00:25:02.629 --> 00:25:07.134
clearly. I don't know anything.

511
00:25:11.104 --> 00:25:12.639
[sighs]

512
00:25:14.274 --> 00:25:16.076
[Calvin]
We'll give you a moment.

513
00:25:21.882 --> 00:25:23.383
[quiet sobs]

514
00:25:24.317 --> 00:25:25.185
[door closes]

515
00:25:25.285 --> 00:25:27.487
Well. that was brutal.

516
00:25:27.587 --> 00:25:29.522
Well. we had to tell her
the truth.

517
00:25:29.622 --> 00:25:31.024
I know.

518
00:25:31.124 --> 00:25:33.626
And we just unraveled
a marriage. and we still

519
00:25:33.726 --> 00:25:35.495
don't have answers.

520
00:25:35.595 --> 00:25:38.198
Maybe Blake's hard drive
will help.

521
00:25:38.298 --> 00:25:39.833
My man.

522
00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:42.602
Let me see.

523
00:25:44.804 --> 00:25:46.839
Fallon. you want some company?

524
00:25:46.840 --> 00:25:49.476
[Fallon] No. Just... [sighs]
give me a minute.

525
00:25:49.576 --> 00:25:50.677
[door opens]

526
00:25:50.810 --> 00:25:52.545
- [sighs]
- [door closes]

527
00:25:53.947 --> 00:25:57.183
Poor kid. She's literally
worried sick about her dad.

528
00:25:57.184 --> 00:25:59.018
Given that Blake was
grabbed nearby.

529
00:25:59.019 --> 00:26:00.353
Cal wants us to clear out.

530
00:26:01.154 --> 00:26:03.223
All Fallon knows
is that her father's missing.

531
00:26:03.323 --> 00:26:04.824
That's all she needs to know.

532
00:26:05.893 --> 00:26:08.929
♪ suspenseful music ♪

533
00:26:10.964 --> 00:26:15.402
We found some information
we'd like to share with you.

534
00:26:15.535 --> 00:26:17.905
Your husband attended
the opening of a clinic

535
00:26:18.005 --> 00:26:20.974
in Equatorial Guinea
about six months ago. right?

536
00:26:21.074 --> 00:26:22.542
- Yes.
- That clinic

537
00:26:22.642 --> 00:26:24.577
was run by Luis Andeme.

538
00:26:24.677 --> 00:26:27.180
He's an activist
against the repressive regime

539
00:26:27.280 --> 00:26:28.715
of President Bindong.

540
00:26:28.848 --> 00:26:30.951
So this is payback for Blake
giving medical supplies

541
00:26:31.051 --> 00:26:32.920
to the resistance?

542
00:26:33.053 --> 00:26:34.487
That hard drive contains

543
00:26:34.587 --> 00:26:38.090
evidence showing Andeme
convinced Blake to use his

544
00:26:38.091 --> 00:26:40.660
nonprofit infrastructure to
smuggle weapons for his cause.

545
00:26:40.760 --> 00:26:42.762
What?

546
00:26:42.862 --> 00:26:47.067
You-You're telling me
Blake's an arms dealer?

547
00:26:47.167 --> 00:26:51.237
President Bindong's daughter
was killed last month. Car bomb.

548
00:26:51.238 --> 00:26:54.607
[Belle] Made by the resistance
with explosives

549
00:26:54.741 --> 00:26:57.677
your husband supplied.

550
00:26:59.412 --> 00:27:01.982
And then. three days ago.
Blake received

551
00:27:02.082 --> 00:27:04.584
e-mails from Bindong's henchmen.
threatening death

552
00:27:04.684 --> 00:27:06.386
unless he turned over
information

553
00:27:06.486 --> 00:27:09.722
about everyone
he has shipped weapons to.

554
00:27:10.757 --> 00:27:13.860
[Calvin] Blake probably
overheard us discussing

555
00:27:13.961 --> 00:27:16.529
the construction of the car
bomb. and he connected the dots.

556
00:27:16.629 --> 00:27:18.031
contacted them to meet.

557
00:27:18.131 --> 00:27:21.101
Trying to protect
you and Fallon.

558
00:27:21.234 --> 00:27:24.104
[Calvin]
And when they get

559
00:27:24.204 --> 00:27:26.439
what they need from him...

560
00:27:27.574 --> 00:27:29.977
Can't you identify
these monsters?

561
00:27:30.077 --> 00:27:32.645
FRS returns identities
that seem to be scrubbed

562
00:27:32.745 --> 00:27:34.147
in ways often seen with people

563
00:27:34.247 --> 00:27:36.315
who've done covert work
with the U.S. government.

564
00:27:36.316 --> 00:27:38.485
♪ tense. dramatic music ♪

565
00:27:38.618 --> 00:27:40.920
Their files can be unclassified

566
00:27:41.021 --> 00:27:44.124
with a warrant
signed by a federal judge.

567
00:27:45.592 --> 00:27:47.427
Shall we?

568
00:27:47.527 --> 00:27:49.829
- [raining]
- [thunder rumbling]

569
00:27:55.435 --> 00:27:57.670
Finding you a secure location.

570
00:27:58.471 --> 00:28:00.440
And my mom's worried
about a concert.

571
00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:01.974
On it. Cal.

572
00:28:01.975 --> 00:28:03.876
Guys in the red van
are Americans...

573
00:28:03.977 --> 00:28:05.844
Rylan Hightower and Nate Porter.

574
00:28:05.845 --> 00:28:07.680
Ex-Delta Force.
now private contractors.

575
00:28:07.814 --> 00:28:11.251
They both did FID
for Bindong's forces in 2022.

576
00:28:12.019 --> 00:28:13.685
Is their contracting group
out of Texas?

577
00:28:13.686 --> 00:28:16.523
Unknown. but Hightower has
property near Clyde Park.

578
00:28:16.623 --> 00:28:18.491
That might be
where they're headed.

579
00:28:18.591 --> 00:28:20.660
[Kayce] That's only
a few miles from here.

580
00:28:25.398 --> 00:28:28.068
What do we do about...

581
00:28:28.835 --> 00:28:31.204
Blake doesn't have much time.

582
00:28:32.172 --> 00:28:33.506
[sighs]

583
00:28:33.606 --> 00:28:35.842
♪ tense. dramatic music ♪

584
00:28:59.999 --> 00:29:03.070
- This is where my dad is?
- We're about to find out.

585
00:29:03.170 --> 00:29:05.372
I can't handle this.
I'm freaking out.

586
00:29:06.139 --> 00:29:09.409
[Andrea]
Fallon. it's gonna be okay.

587
00:29:10.310 --> 00:29:13.180
DOJ wants to talk to these guys
about their work with Bindong.

588
00:29:13.280 --> 00:29:15.581
so we need them alive.

589
00:29:15.582 --> 00:29:17.250
Blake doesn't have time.

590
00:29:17.384 --> 00:29:19.352
I'm going in now.
You stay with Fallon.

591
00:29:19.452 --> 00:29:20.720
One is none. remember?

592
00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:22.555
Especially against
special forces operators.

593
00:29:22.655 --> 00:29:24.491
Cal and Belle are
ten minutes out.

594
00:29:26.659 --> 00:29:28.428
You ever wish that help
would've gotten to your dad

595
00:29:28.561 --> 00:29:29.962
ten minutes faster?

596
00:29:32.265 --> 00:29:34.134
- [truck door opens]
- [exhales]

597
00:29:46.846 --> 00:29:49.482
♪ suspenseful music ♪

598
00:29:51.384 --> 00:29:55.388
[Porter] Give us some names
or fry some more.

599
00:29:56.456 --> 00:29:57.624
[Blake]
Please. I told you.

600
00:29:57.724 --> 00:30:00.127
I don't know. I don't know.

601
00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:01.361
Let's help him remember. yeah?

602
00:30:01.461 --> 00:30:03.396
U.S. Marshals!

603
00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:10.470
[Blake grunting]

604
00:30:10.570 --> 00:30:12.839
[Kayce]
You okay?

605
00:30:12.939 --> 00:30:15.942
I will be
when you get the other guy.

606
00:30:17.344 --> 00:30:19.579
♪ intense. dramatic music ♪

607
00:30:19.679 --> 00:30:21.348
[gunshots]

608
00:30:42.302 --> 00:30:45.138
[both grunting]

609
00:30:53.246 --> 00:30:54.647
[coughs]

610
00:31:03.790 --> 00:31:05.892
[panting]

611
00:31:12.899 --> 00:31:14.167
[Calvin exhales]

612
00:31:14.267 --> 00:31:16.068
It's just here.

613
00:31:20.507 --> 00:31:21.941
[sighs]

614
00:31:22.041 --> 00:31:23.675
Oh. thank God.

615
00:31:23.676 --> 00:31:26.446
♪ gentle music ♪

616
00:31:37.690 --> 00:31:40.126
You haven't said a word
to your dad.

617
00:31:40.227 --> 00:31:41.893
What do I say?

618
00:31:41.894 --> 00:31:44.564
Thanks for nearly getting Mom
shot and blown up?

619
00:31:44.664 --> 00:31:46.533
I'd just be grateful
they're alive.

620
00:31:46.666 --> 00:31:48.201
I am.

621
00:31:48.335 --> 00:31:49.702
But...

622
00:31:50.503 --> 00:31:52.439
...is my dad a monster?

623
00:31:54.974 --> 00:31:59.078
I once took down this fugitive
my dad had put away.

624
00:31:59.912 --> 00:32:02.047
The guy swore
my old man was corrupt.

625
00:32:02.048 --> 00:32:04.050
It shook me up.

626
00:32:04.150 --> 00:32:06.018
Do you think he was dirty?

627
00:32:06.118 --> 00:32:08.821
I think that I would
love the chance to ask him.

628
00:32:10.122 --> 00:32:11.658
No father's perfect.

629
00:32:12.559 --> 00:32:14.193
And once you realize he was just
trying to protect you

630
00:32:14.294 --> 00:32:17.297
in his own messed-up way.
your anger will fade.

631
00:32:18.365 --> 00:32:20.899
I just hope that. if you ever
do decide to forgive him.

632
00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:23.470
he's still around to hear it.

633
00:32:47.727 --> 00:32:48.628
Hey.

634
00:32:48.761 --> 00:32:49.961
Hey.

635
00:32:49.962 --> 00:32:51.597
[Belle]
I just closed the Ayers file.

636
00:32:51.598 --> 00:32:55.167
Should we go join the others
at the Bullet?

637
00:32:55.268 --> 00:32:56.903
Pass.

638
00:32:57.003 --> 00:32:59.606
[sighs] Come on.

639
00:32:59.706 --> 00:33:01.541
Is Maddie still
freezing you out?

640
00:33:01.641 --> 00:33:03.376
You know. one of us
can order for you.

641
00:33:03.476 --> 00:33:07.847
avoid any further
awkward interactions.

642
00:33:09.215 --> 00:33:11.818
Look. go have fun
with your teammates.

643
00:33:13.486 --> 00:33:15.488
Well. this is a pickle.

644
00:33:16.323 --> 00:33:19.125
See. I really need
that buffer zone

645
00:33:19.258 --> 00:33:22.128
between work and home
that you suggested.

646
00:33:22.228 --> 00:33:24.664
but I can't leave you here
like this.

647
00:33:27.133 --> 00:33:30.437
Bourbon? [whistles]
That's an aggressive choice.

648
00:33:31.304 --> 00:33:35.575
Man. we just told the judge
half her life is a lie.

649
00:33:35.675 --> 00:33:37.810
Move.

650
00:33:37.910 --> 00:33:40.079
I mean. if that doesn't call
for hard stuff...

651
00:33:42.749 --> 00:33:44.351
...I don't know what does.

652
00:33:44.484 --> 00:33:46.686
[rock music playing]

653
00:33:49.422 --> 00:33:52.859
<i>♪ A soul that can't be tamed ♪</i>

654
00:33:52.992 --> 00:33:56.796
<i>♪ An open road
that calls our names... ♪</i>

655
00:33:57.564 --> 00:33:59.366
[Miles] <i>Dedicate your life
to someone. only to find out</i>

656
00:33:59.499 --> 00:34:00.933
you barely know 'em.

657
00:34:01.033 --> 00:34:03.535
[sighs] A family like that
is the reason why

658
00:34:03.536 --> 00:34:05.071
I remain eternally single.

659
00:34:05.171 --> 00:34:06.473
[Miles]
Bulldogger's loss.

660
00:34:06.573 --> 00:34:08.039
- [Andrea chuckles]
- What's next for you?

661
00:34:08.040 --> 00:34:09.609
Bull rider? Rodeo clown?

662
00:34:09.709 --> 00:34:13.679
No. What about you? When are you
asking out this mystery girl?

663
00:34:13.680 --> 00:34:16.315
Probably too complicated
for it to ever work out.

664
00:34:16.416 --> 00:34:18.284
That's how you know it's right.

665
00:34:18.385 --> 00:34:21.588
I don't have a lot of experience
dating non-Native women.

666
00:34:21.688 --> 00:34:22.889
Just be confident.

667
00:34:22.989 --> 00:34:24.524
[Miles]
Not exactly my strong suit.

668
00:34:24.624 --> 00:34:27.860
Any advice on asking out
women around here from a local?

669
00:34:27.960 --> 00:34:29.496
Well. the last time
I asked out anyone.

670
00:34:29.596 --> 00:34:31.431
I was in high school
and she was from Broken Rock.

671
00:34:32.298 --> 00:34:33.866
If I'm gonna crash and burn.

672
00:34:33.966 --> 00:34:37.036
might as well have my teammates
here to put out the flames.

673
00:34:39.439 --> 00:34:40.707
She's here?

674
00:34:40.807 --> 00:34:42.542
Here goes nothing.

675
00:34:42.642 --> 00:34:44.577
<i>♪ Mm. sit still ♪</i>

676
00:34:44.677 --> 00:34:47.747
<i>♪ But got hard to leave.
ooh-way ♪</i>

677
00:34:47.847 --> 00:34:51.851
<i>♪ There's nothing out there
that can make her stay ♪</i>

678
00:34:51.951 --> 00:34:53.886
<i>♪ Be gone world... ♪</i>

679
00:34:53.986 --> 00:34:55.422
You guys need refills?

680
00:34:55.555 --> 00:34:57.089
[Miles]
Um. sure.

681
00:34:57.189 --> 00:34:59.058
[chuckles]

682
00:34:59.158 --> 00:35:00.893
Also. uh...

683
00:35:01.027 --> 00:35:03.029
I was wondering.

684
00:35:03.129 --> 00:35:05.398
would you maybe like to go
on a date sometime?

685
00:35:06.399 --> 00:35:07.433
With you?

686
00:35:07.434 --> 00:35:08.900
Maybe.

687
00:35:08.901 --> 00:35:10.436
I mean...

688
00:35:10.437 --> 00:35:12.371
yeah. with me.

689
00:35:12.472 --> 00:35:14.774
Yeah. I-I'd love to.

690
00:35:14.874 --> 00:35:17.109
[chuckles] I was hoping
you might be interested.

691
00:35:17.243 --> 00:35:21.246
I just thought maybe
you'd chicken out.

692
00:35:21.247 --> 00:35:23.949
No way. I'm a confident guy.

693
00:35:23.950 --> 00:35:27.620
Well. you must be.
asking out your boss's daughter.

694
00:35:27.754 --> 00:35:29.922
<i>♪ Loud and sweet ♪</i>

695
00:35:30.022 --> 00:35:32.925
[chuckles]
Maddie was maybe three.

696
00:35:33.025 --> 00:35:34.793
and we went to. we went

697
00:35:34.794 --> 00:35:38.330
to the San Diego Zoo. [laughs]
She lost her mind.

698
00:35:38.431 --> 00:35:39.932
[both laughing]

699
00:35:40.032 --> 00:35:44.136
And I was. I was tucking her in
that night. and...

700
00:35:44.236 --> 00:35:46.973
she said.
"This is the best day ever."

701
00:35:52.745 --> 00:35:55.147
Well. you know.
no one's childhood

702
00:35:55.281 --> 00:35:57.216
stays frozen in time.

703
00:35:57.316 --> 00:35:59.652
Look at Fallon.
She just found out her father's

704
00:35:59.752 --> 00:36:02.254
the villain
in someone else's story.

705
00:36:02.354 --> 00:36:04.290
What about Pauline?

706
00:36:05.057 --> 00:36:07.994
I mean. Blake wasn't
who she thought he was. either.

707
00:36:08.094 --> 00:36:11.130
- Mm.
- I mean. does their...

708
00:36:11.230 --> 00:36:12.732
does their marriage survive?

709
00:36:12.832 --> 00:36:15.001
[both chuckle]

710
00:36:15.768 --> 00:36:18.505
You know how tough marriage is.

711
00:36:22.174 --> 00:36:24.310
Would your marriage survive
if your...

712
00:36:24.410 --> 00:36:26.078
husband was living
a secret life?

713
00:36:26.178 --> 00:36:28.715
There's nothing
I don't know about Jared.

714
00:36:28.815 --> 00:36:30.282
- [chuckles] Really?
- Really.

715
00:36:30.382 --> 00:36:33.553
Given everything
that you shield from him?

716
00:36:34.420 --> 00:36:36.155
You really think
a cop can't tell

717
00:36:36.255 --> 00:36:37.957
you're sitting on something?

718
00:36:38.057 --> 00:36:39.826
Come on. Out with it.

719
00:36:39.926 --> 00:36:43.530
You have been weird all day.
Give it to me.

720
00:36:43.630 --> 00:36:46.331
Look. it's not my place.

721
00:36:46.332 --> 00:36:48.400
but I-I know that you would do
the same for me

722
00:36:48.501 --> 00:36:50.402
if the situations
were reversed. so...

723
00:36:50.503 --> 00:36:52.739
♪ dramatic music ♪

724
00:36:57.043 --> 00:36:59.746
What situation?

725
00:37:04.350 --> 00:37:06.853
I saw Jared with another woman.

726
00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:15.695
[sighs]

727
00:37:19.298 --> 00:37:22.101
He's supposed to be discreet.

728
00:37:23.069 --> 00:37:26.237
What? Wait. that's it?

729
00:37:26.238 --> 00:37:29.207
[sighs] Okay.

730
00:37:29.208 --> 00:37:33.044
Not that I have
to justify anything.

731
00:37:33.045 --> 00:37:34.914
but...

732
00:37:36.048 --> 00:37:38.551
...people change.

733
00:37:38.651 --> 00:37:40.553
You know. years go by.

734
00:37:40.687 --> 00:37:43.790
My work undercover
kept us apart.

735
00:37:45.024 --> 00:37:49.729
Things slipped... away.

736
00:37:50.930 --> 00:37:52.965
Why... why stay together?

737
00:37:53.065 --> 00:37:55.835
Keeping my family whole
for Braxton

738
00:37:55.935 --> 00:37:59.772
is my priority.

739
00:37:59.872 --> 00:38:01.140
[sighs]

740
00:38:01.240 --> 00:38:03.743
Seems kind of lonely.
though. no?

741
00:38:25.231 --> 00:38:26.932
[laughing]
That was a terrible idea.

742
00:38:26.933 --> 00:38:31.137
[chuckles] Yeah. Sorry. uh.
the-the booze and long day.

743
00:38:31.237 --> 00:38:34.173
[sighs] Yeah. Uh...

744
00:38:35.441 --> 00:38:36.776
Let's just call it a night.

745
00:38:37.610 --> 00:38:39.979
["His to Mine"
by Adam Sanders playing]

746
00:38:47.887 --> 00:38:51.190
<i>♪ If he's anything like me ♪</i>

747
00:38:51.290 --> 00:38:55.027
<i>♪ That old boy
had to see it coming... ♪</i>

748
00:38:55.127 --> 00:38:57.529
[both laughing]

749
00:38:57.630 --> 00:38:58.665
<i>♪ And if you ask... ♪</i>

750
00:38:58.765 --> 00:38:59.799
Guy who doesn't drink

751
00:38:59.932 --> 00:39:01.433
pining for the bartender.
Go figure.

752
00:39:01.533 --> 00:39:05.171
<i>♪ Anything.
I bet he doesn't... ♪</i>

753
00:39:06.005 --> 00:39:08.339
You really haven't
asked anyone out since Monica?

754
00:39:08.340 --> 00:39:12.478
<i>♪ I bet he's why your phone's
face down on the bar... ♪</i>

755
00:39:12.578 --> 00:39:14.013
Did your mom date
after your dad?

756
00:39:14.146 --> 00:39:15.447
<i>♪ If he was here
he'd tell me... ♪</i>

757
00:39:15.547 --> 00:39:17.849
Oh. now we're getting somewhere.

758
00:39:17.850 --> 00:39:19.451
[chuckles] Does this have
anything to do

759
00:39:19.551 --> 00:39:21.519
with the Weaver Ranch swag
at your house?

760
00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:23.289
Hey. Dolly ambushed me.

761
00:39:23.389 --> 00:39:24.523
[laughs] Really?

762
00:39:24.657 --> 00:39:26.292
Drive-by date?

763
00:39:26.392 --> 00:39:28.527
Oh. I underestimated this chick.

764
00:39:28.627 --> 00:39:30.162
<i>♪ A girl like you puts... ♪</i>

765
00:39:30.296 --> 00:39:33.031
Did you enjoy it?

766
00:39:33.032 --> 00:39:36.869
As much as you and I focus
on avenging our dead...

767
00:39:36.969 --> 00:39:38.971
guess we can betray them. too.

768
00:39:39.772 --> 00:39:42.842
Hanging out with Dolly
felt like cheating on Monica.

769
00:39:43.943 --> 00:39:44.844
I see.

770
00:39:44.977 --> 00:39:47.246
<i>♪ Worth the ride... ♪</i>

771
00:39:47.346 --> 00:39:48.781
Yeah. my mom dated.

772
00:39:48.881 --> 00:39:50.349
Then she met a great guy.

773
00:39:50.482 --> 00:39:52.051
and I realized

774
00:39:52.151 --> 00:39:54.887
that she wasn't replacing my dad
in her heart.

775
00:39:55.021 --> 00:39:58.224
she was just making room
for someone new.

776
00:40:00.526 --> 00:40:01.694
What about your dad?

777
00:40:01.794 --> 00:40:04.196
<i>♪ Baby. take me to heaven... ♪</i>

778
00:40:04.296 --> 00:40:06.231
Uh. nothing serious.

779
00:40:06.232 --> 00:40:09.535
He didn't have room
for anyone or anything else

780
00:40:09.668 --> 00:40:11.804
other than anger
at losing my mom.

781
00:40:12.805 --> 00:40:15.240
And do you think Monica
would want that for you?

782
00:40:15.241 --> 00:40:17.710
<i>♪ Just hit me
with that hurt... ♪</i>

783
00:40:17.810 --> 00:40:19.178
I'd love the chance to ask her.

784
00:40:19.278 --> 00:40:22.815
<i>♪ Before me. wherever he is ♪</i>

785
00:40:22.915 --> 00:40:26.251
<i>♪ In the world tonight ♪</i>

786
00:40:26.252 --> 00:40:29.655
<i>♪ I bet he's picking up pieces ♪</i>

787
00:40:30.522 --> 00:40:32.590
<i>♪ A girl like you ♪</i>

788
00:40:32.591 --> 00:40:35.361
<i>♪ Puts the good in goodbye ♪</i>

789
00:40:35.461 --> 00:40:38.998
<i>♪ I bet you make it
look easy... ♪</i>

790
00:40:39.098 --> 00:40:40.432
[horse neighing]

791
00:40:43.870 --> 00:40:45.504
[exhales]

792
00:41:10.797 --> 00:41:13.165
You gonna get back
on that horse?

793
00:41:14.433 --> 00:41:16.602
Not sure I'm ready.

794
00:41:17.837 --> 00:41:20.039
I'm sorry about the other night.
I think I overstepped.

795
00:41:20.139 --> 00:41:22.108
Call it a family trait.

796
00:41:24.877 --> 00:41:27.646
Is another tour
out of the question?

797
00:41:28.781 --> 00:41:31.717
It's just a horseback ride.

798
00:41:34.153 --> 00:41:39.391
<i>♪ Yeah. I know my heart
don't stand a chance tonight ♪</i>

799
00:41:39.491 --> 00:41:43.629
<i>♪ But do what you did to his ♪</i>

800
00:41:43.729 --> 00:41:46.165
<i>♪ It's yours for the breaking ♪</i>

801
00:41:46.265 --> 00:41:48.767
<i>♪ Girl. I'll be just fine ♪</i>

802
00:41:48.868 --> 00:41:53.305
<i>♪ So do what you did to his ♪</i>

803
00:41:53.405 --> 00:41:56.175
<i>♪ To mine ♪</i>

804
00:41:57.977 --> 00:42:02.548
<i>♪ Yeah. to mine ♪</i>

805
00:42:11.357 --> 00:42:13.659
♪ intense. percussive music ♪

